Subject: thermald: fix v2.15.10 -> v2.5.10 tag typo

The thermald element pins its ref to v2.15.10-0-g88369b42... No such
tag exists at intel/thermal_daemon. The upstream repo's latest tag is
v2.5.13, and sha 88369b42... (per the GitHub API) is tagged v2.5.10,
not v2.15.10 — looks like a typo in gnome-build-meta that prior builds
never reached because earlier fetches of m17n-db (from the flaky
savannah mirror) failed the workflow before this element got a shot.

Correcting the ref so the git_repo plugin's tag-verification step
matches the real tag. Commit sha is unchanged.

diff --git a/elements/gnomeos-deps/thermald.bst b/elements/gnomeos-deps/thermald.bst
--- a/elements/gnomeos-deps/thermald.bst
+++ b/elements/gnomeos-deps/thermald.bst
@@ -4,7 +4,7 @@ sources:
 - kind: git_repo
   url: github:intel/thermal_daemon.git
   track: "v*"
-  ref: v2.15.10-0-g88369b42ec523787081b9bf8811b364e2a3d5f2d
+  ref: v2.5.10-0-g88369b42ec523787081b9bf8811b364e2a3d5f2d

 build-depends:
